{"assessment":"The source provides a quantitative study of disorder-free localization (DFL) in a non-Abelian SU(2) lattice gauge theory. The best quantitative cluster is the entanglement entropy scaling in the SS and GI sectors at fixed mass m=1 and gauge coupling g^2=15, with fits S_SS = 2.94(2) log(t) + 1.33(3) and S_GI = 0.386(6) t + 0.43(2). This provides a numeric control (time t), a single shared numeric readout (time-averaged half-chain bipartite entropy), quantitative mechanisms (logarithmic and linear growth), and an explicit domain (t in [2,5] from reviewer evidence). The case is authoring-ready.","case_authoring_ready":true,"claims":[{"anchors":[{"line_end":263,"line_start":263,"support":"SS case exhibits a clear linear entanglement growth in log(t) across almost all the coupling values, compatible with an MBL phase."},{"line_end":776,"line_start":776,"support":"Logarithmic fit of SS curve: S_SS=2.94(2)log(t)+1.33(3)"}],"applicability":"The logarithmic growth is observed across almost all coupling values in [0,15] at fixed mass m=1, but the explicit fit is at g^2=15. The fit is valid for the SS initial state under periodic boundary conditions.","claim_id":"SS_entropy_log_growth","control_domains":[{"allowed_values":[],"anchors":[{"line_end":803,"line_start":801,"support":"Reviewer figure evidence: the two displayed fitted relations share the axis-interior interval from t=2 through t=5."}],"control_name":"t","domain_kind":"continuous_interval","domain_statement":"Conservative common interval t in [2,5] for the two displayed fitted relations, as supported by reviewer figure evidence.","maximum":5.0,"minimum":2.0}],"control_names":["t"],"depends_on":[],"fixed_condition_ids":["N8_PBC","mass_fixed_1","g2_fixed_15","hardcore_gluon_truncation","half_chain_entropy_definition","time_averaging_window","SS_initial_state"],"mechanism_ids":["log_entropy_growth_SS"],"oracle_outputs":{"time_averaged_half_chain_entropy":{"args":[{"args":[{"param":"slope_SS_log_fit"},{"args":[{"var":"t"}],"op":"log"}],"op":"multiply"},{"param":"intercept_SS_log_fit"}],"op":"add"}},"quantitative_form":"S_SS = 2.94 * log(t) + 1.33","readout_names":["time_averaged_half_chain_entropy"],"statement":"For the SS initial state at fixed mass m=1 and gauge coupling g^2=15, the time-averaged half-chain bipartite entanglement entropy grows logarithmically with time, with a fitted relation S_SS = 2.94(2) log(t) + 1.33(3).","statistical_basis":"Fit to the time-dependent entanglement entropy curve at g^2=15; fit parameters reported with uncertainties 0.02 and 0.03, convention unspecified.","uncertainty":"Fit parameter uncertainties: slope 0.02, intercept 0.03, convention source_unspecified."},{"anchors":[{"line_end":764,"line_start":764,"support":"This is exactly what we observe for the GI sector across all coupling regimes compatible with ergodicity."},{"line_end":776,"line_start":776,"support":"Linear fit of GI curve: S_GI=0.386(6)*t+0.43(2)"}],"applicability":"The linear growth is observed across all coupling regimes compatible with ergodicity at fixed mass m=1, with the explicit fit at g^2=15. The fit is valid for the GI initial state under periodic boundary conditions.","claim_id":"GI_entropy_linear_growth","control_domains":[{"allowed_values":[],"anchors":[{"line_end":803,"line_start":801,"support":"Reviewer figure evidence: the two displayed fitted relations share the axis-interior interval from t=2 through t=5."}],"control_name":"t","domain_kind":"continuous_interval","domain_statement":"Conservative common interval t in [2,5] for the two displayed fitted relations, as supported by reviewer figure evidence.","maximum":5.0,"minimum":2.0}],"control_names":["t"],"depends_on":[],"fixed_condition_ids":["N8_PBC","mass_fixed_1","g2_fixed_15","hardcore_gluon_truncation","half_chain_entropy_definition","time_averaging_window","GI_initial_state"],"mechanism_ids":["linear_entropy_growth_GI"],"oracle_outputs":{"time_averaged_half_chain_entropy":{"args":[{"args":[{"param":"slope_GI_linear_fit"},{"var":"t"}],"op":"multiply"},{"param":"intercept_GI_linear_fit"}],"op":"add"}},"quantitative_form":"S_GI = 0.386 * t + 0.43","readout_names":["time_averaged_half_chain_entropy"],"statement":"For the GI initial state at fixed mass m=1 and gauge coupling g^2=15, the time-averaged half-chain bipartite entanglement entropy grows linearly with time, with a fitted relation S_GI = 0.386(6) t + 0.43(2).","statistical_basis":"Fit to the time-dependent entanglement entropy curve at g^2=15; fit parameters reported with uncertainties 0.006 and 0.02, convention unspecified.","uncertainty":"Fit parameter uncertainties: slope 0.006, intercept 0.02, convention source_unspecified."}],"controls":[{"allowed_values":[],"anchors":[{"line_end":803,"line_start":801,"support":"Reviewer figure evidence: the two displayed fitted relations share the axis-interior interval from t=2 through t=5."}],"definition":"Time in the time-averaged entanglement entropy evolution.","domain_kind":"continuous_interval","domain_statement":"Conservative common interval t in [2,5] for the two displayed fitted relations, as supported by reviewer figure evidence.","maximum":5.0,"minimum":2.0,"name":"t","unit":"dimensionless (lattice units)"}],"fixed_conditions":[{"anchors":[{"line_end":161,"line_start":161,"support":"Use exact diagonalization on a chain of N=8 SU(2) dressed sites with periodic boundary conditions."}],"condition_id":"N8_PBC","statement":"Chain of N=8 SU(2) dressed sites with periodic boundary conditions."},{"anchors":[{"line_end":775,"line_start":775,"support":"Time-averaged half-chain bipartite entanglement entropy in base two as a function of time for fixed mass m=1."}],"condition_id":"mass_fixed_1","statement":"Fixed mass m=1."},{"anchors":[{"line_end":776,"line_start":776,"support":"The cyan dashed lines correspond to (a) the linear fit of the (g^2=15) GI curve and (b) the logarithmic fit of the (g^2=15) SS curve."}],"condition_id":"g2_fixed_15","statement":"Fixed gauge coupling g^2=15."},{"anchors":[{"line_end":140,"line_start":140,"support":"Implement hardcore-gluon truncation and restrict spin in {0,1/2}."},{"line_end":157,"line_start":157,"support":"Restricting to first two irreps, i.e., spin_b in {0,1/2} is sufficient to detect DFL."}],"condition_id":"hardcore_gluon_truncation","statement":"Hardcore-gluon truncation restricting gauge link spin to {0,1/2} and background charge spin to {0,1/2}."},{"anchors":[{"line_end":261,"line_start":261,"support":"Bipartite von Neumann entanglement entropy defined as S = -Tr[rho_A log rho_A]."},{"line_end":775,"line_start":775,"support":"Time-averaged half-chain bipartite entanglement entropy in base two."}],"condition_id":"half_chain_entropy_definition","statement":"Half-chain bipartite von Neumann entanglement entropy in base two, defined as S = -Tr[rho_A log rho_A] with A being half of the chain."},{"anchors":[{"line_end":767,"line_start":767,"support":"Time-averaged entanglement entropy over a window Delta t = 2.5."}],"condition_id":"time_averaging_window","statement":"Time-averaged entanglement entropy over a window Delta t = 2.5."},{"anchors":[{"line_end":179,"line_start":173,"support":"Initialize dynamics from equal superposition of all N_SS gauge superselection sectors (SS) of background-charges: |Psi_SS> = (1/sqrt(N_SS)) sum_kappa |Psi_{b^kappa_site}> with b^kappa_site in {0,1/2}."}],"condition_id":"SS_initial_state","statement":"Initial state is the equal superposition of all gauge superselection sectors (SS) as defined in Eq. (3)."},{"anchors":[{"line_end":193,"line_start":187,"support":"For direct comparison, we also consider the same matter configuration of the state in Eq. (3) with no active gauge fields, which belongs to the gauge-invariant (GI) sector without background charges."}],"condition_id":"GI_initial_state","statement":"Initial state is the gauge-invariant state without background charges, as defined in Eq. (4)."}],"mechanisms":[{"anchors":[{"line_end":263,"line_start":263,"support":"SS case exhibits a clear linear entanglement growth in log(t) across almost all the coupling values, compatible with an MBL phase."},{"line_end":776,"line_start":776,"support":"Logarithmic fit of SS curve: S_SS=2.94(2)log(t)+1.33(3)"}],"equations":["S_SS = 2.94(2) * log(t) + 1.33(3)"],"mechanism_id":"log_entropy_growth_SS","parameters":[{"anchors":[{"line_end":776,"line_start":776,"support":"Logarithmic fit of SS curve: S_SS=2.94(2)log(t)+1.33(3)"}],"name":"slope_SS_log_fit","role":"slope of logarithmic fit of entanglement entropy vs log(t) in SS sector at g^2=15","uncertainty":"0.02 (source_unspecified)","unit":"dimensionless","value":2.94},{"anchors":[{"line_end":776,"line_start":776,"support":"Logarithmic fit of SS curve: S_SS=2.94(2)log(t)+1.33(3)"}],"name":"intercept_SS_log_fit","role":"intercept of logarithmic fit of entanglement entropy vs log(t) in SS sector at g^2=15","uncertainty":"0.03 (source_unspecified)","unit":"dimensionless","value":1.33}],"statement":"In the SS sector, the half-chain bipartite entanglement entropy grows logarithmically with time, compatible with many-body localization, with a linear fit in log(t) at g^2=15.","variable_names":["S_SS","t","g^2"]},{"anchors":[{"line_end":764,"line_start":764,"support":"This is exactly what we observe for the GI sector across all coupling regimes compatible with ergodicity."},{"line_end":776,"line_start":776,"support":"Linear fit of GI curve: S_GI=0.386(6)*t+0.43(2)"}],"equations":["S_GI = 0.386(6) * t + 0.43(2)"],"mechanism_id":"linear_entropy_growth_GI","parameters":[{"anchors":[{"line_end":776,"line_start":776,"support":"Linear fit of GI curve: S_GI=0.386(6)*t+0.43(2)"}],"name":"slope_GI_linear_fit","role":"slope of linear fit of entanglement entropy vs time in GI sector at g^2=15","uncertainty":"0.006 (source_unspecified)","unit":"dimensionless","value":0.386},{"anchors":[{"line_end":776,"line_start":776,"support":"Linear fit of GI curve: S_GI=0.386(6)*t+0.43(2)"}],"name":"intercept_GI_linear_fit","role":"intercept of linear fit of entanglement entropy vs time in GI sector at g^2=15","uncertainty":"0.02 (source_unspecified)","unit":"dimensionless","value":0.43}],"statement":"In the GI sector, the half-chain bipartite entanglement entropy grows linearly with time, compatible with ergodicity, with a linear fit at g^2=15.","variable_names":["S_GI","t","g^2"]}],"paper_scope":"The paper investigates dynamical phases of a (1+1)D truncated SU(2) lattice gauge theory with dynamical matter, focusing on disorder-free localization (DFL), Hilbert space fragmentation (HSF), and ergodic behavior. It uses exact diagonalization on an N=8 site chain with periodic boundary conditions, and studies matter imbalance, quark populations, and entanglement entropy scaling.","readouts":[{"anchors":[{"line_end":775,"line_start":775,"support":"Time-averaged half-chain bipartite entanglement entropy in base two as a function of time for fixed mass m=1, and a range of gauge couplings g^2 in [0,15] in (a) the gauge-invariant (GI) and (b) superposition of superselection (SS) sectors."},{"line_end":776,"line_start":776,"support":"The cyan dashed lines correspond to (a) the linear fit of the (g^2=15) GI curve S_GI=0.386(6)*t+0.43(2) and (b) the logarithmic fit of the (g^2=15) SS curve S_SS=2.94(2)log(t)+1.33(3)."}],"definition":"Time-averaged half-chain bipartite von Neumann entanglement entropy in base two, defined as S = -Tr[rho_A log rho_A] with A being half of the chain.","name":"time_averaged_half_chain_entropy","resolution":null,"statistic":"Time-averaged over a window Delta t = 2.5.","uncertainty":"Fit parameters have uncertainties with unspecified convention (source_unspecified).","unit":"dimensionless (bits)"}],"source":{"arxiv_versioned_id":"2505.04704v2","citation":"Giovanni Cataldi, Disorder-Free Localization and Fragmentation in a Non-Abelian Lattice Gauge Theory, Physical Review Letters (2026), DOI:10.1103/fhfy-dh85","journal_doi":"10.1103/fhfy-dh85"},"source_ambiguities":[]}
